Jolimark FP-620K+ CUPS driver
=============================

This package installs the CUPS filter, backend and PPD.  It does not create
a print queue automatically, because a package should not change the user's
printer configuration without asking.

Create or update the queue with:

    sudo fp620kp-setup

To make it the system default printer and print the calibration page:

    sudo fp620kp-setup --default --test

The setup helper looks for /dev/usb/lp0 first.  If your printer is bound to a
different node, pass it explicitly:

    sudo fp620kp-setup --device /dev/usb/lp1

The queue name defaults to FP620K; use --name to change it.

You can also add the printer through the desktop printer settings or the CUPS
web interface at http://localhost:631/.  The PPD is installed as
/usr/share/cups/model/jolimark-fp620kp.ppd.

Default job options are 360x180 dpi and unidirectional printing.  Use
"lp -d FP620K -o Resolution=180x180dpi file.pdf" for the faster 180x180 mode,
or "PrintDirection=Bidirectional" if speed matters more than straight lines.
